Nestor in southwestern Greece and contained weapons, jewelry, and four gold 
signet rings. It indicates that the article discusses the excavation process, 
artistic style, and craftsmanship of the rings, and argues that the iconography 
of these gold signet rings provides insights into the ideology and religious 
beliefs of the deceased and his community. The entry lists the full 
citation—Hesperia 85.4 (2016), 627–655—and includes keywords such as Pylos, 
Griffin Warrior, gold rings, and Late Bronze Age, thereby situating the study in
the early Mycenaean/Late Bronze Age Aegean context.",
      "source_ref": "s6"
    }
